WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.305 --> 00:00:03.562
- I didn't realize what
undocumented, or being undocumented

00:00:03.562 --> 00:00:05.713
meant until I got to high school.

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:07.468
- When people are getting
ready to get their

00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:10.171
driving permit, or also
apply to college ...

00:00:10.171 --> 00:00:11.514
- All my friends were getting jobs.

00:00:11.514 --> 00:00:13.134
- But I couldn't because I didn't

00:00:13.134 --> 00:00:15.634
have a Social Security Number.

00:00:19.709 --> 00:00:21.676
- Somthing I realized very young,

00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:23.341
was that getting pulled
over means a lot more

00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:24.509
when you're undocumented,

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:26.838
'cause it can have much
more serious consequences.

00:00:26.838 --> 00:00:28.643
- It can mean separation from your family.

00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:30.391
- We've heard of people that, a ticket

00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:32.063
can lead to deportation.

00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:34.239
- When my friend Ryan ran a stop sign,

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:35.885
and when police pulled us over,

00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:37.635
I would just text everybody I know,

00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:39.812
okay, I'm on this intersection,

00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:42.854
and if I don't text you
back in 10 or 20 minutes,

00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:45.847
call this nonprofit organization.

00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:47.365
- If you're out and you're in the car,

00:00:47.365 --> 00:00:49.988
and you see the police,
you automatically become

00:00:49.988 --> 00:00:54.412
struck with fear because
you just want to be okay.

00:00:54.412 --> 00:00:55.300
- One of the hardest parts is

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.052
knowing that nothing is guaranteed.

00:00:57.052 --> 00:00:58.456
You don't know if you'll come home

00:00:58.456 --> 00:00:59.942
and your parents will be there,

00:00:59.942 --> 00:01:01.511
or if you'll make it home that day.

00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:03.473
- When you leave the house, and you leave

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.108
your parents or your siblings,

00:01:05.108 --> 00:01:07.900
you don't know if that
will be the last time

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.277
that you saw them.

00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:10.820
You don't know if, when
you come back home,

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.022
they'll be there.

00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:13.621
So, you don't know if that last good-bye

00:01:13.621 --> 00:01:15.865
you shared with your
family, be it your mom,

00:01:15.865 --> 00:01:17.805
your brother, your sister, your cousin,

00:01:17.805 --> 00:01:19.443
is the last good-bye that you will share.

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:22.293
You're away, you're at the grocery store,

00:01:22.293 --> 00:01:25.915
you're at school, and you
may not be able to come back,

00:01:25.915 --> 00:01:29.253
or when you do come back, your
parents might not be there.

00:01:29.253 --> 00:01:32.678
The fear and anxiety is
something that you learn,

00:01:32.678 --> 00:01:36.428
and you try to deal with
from a very young age.

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:38.338
- And then there's when
you graduate high school,

00:01:38.338 --> 00:01:39.662
and you've worked your butt off to be able

00:01:39.662 --> 00:01:41.517
to get that 4.0 GPA,

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:43.037
- To get you that scholarship,
that financial aid,

00:01:43.037 --> 00:01:46.372
and once you apply, you realize that ...

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.787
- You might have to withdraw
because they find out

00:01:48.787 --> 00:01:50.836
that you're undocumented,
or you might be forced

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:52.978
to pay out of state
tuition, on top of that,

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:55.561
no financial aid, and
this could possibly mean

00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:59.792
you not being able to any more
go to that school or program.

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:01.604
- You know, as undocumented folks,

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:04.269
you can't really think of
anythings in long term.

00:02:04.269 --> 00:02:06.722
There has never really
been a sense of stability,

00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:09.795
and sometimes it's hard
to invest yourselves,

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:12.788
because, in my mind, I
never knew, in five years,

00:02:12.788 --> 00:02:15.228
in a year, in a couple
months, where will I be.

00:02:15.228 --> 00:02:16.853
So, it's hard to plan ahead for life

00:02:16.853 --> 00:02:20.103
and it's hard to work toward something.

00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:27.972
- [President Obama] This
morning, Secretary Napolitano

00:02:27.972 --> 00:02:30.998
announced new actions my
administration will take

00:02:30.998 --> 00:02:34.736
to mend our nation's immigration policy,

00:02:34.736 --> 00:02:39.507
to make it more fair, more
efficient, and more just.

00:02:39.507 --> 00:02:41.729
Specifically, for certain young people,

00:02:41.729 --> 00:02:44.605
sometimes called Dreamers.

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:48.263
Now, these are young people
who study in our schools,

00:02:48.263 --> 00:02:51.350
they play in our
neighborhoods, they're friends

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.517
with our kids; they pledge
allegiance to our flag.

00:02:57.192 --> 00:03:01.086
They are Americans in their
heart, in their minds,

00:03:01.086 --> 00:03:04.164
in every single way but one.

00:03:04.164 --> 00:03:05.499
On paper.

00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:07.275
- So after several years of advocating

00:03:07.275 --> 00:03:09.148
and pushing for a piece of legislation,

00:03:09.148 --> 00:03:12.389
2012 comes around and we
finally have a program

00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:14.131
for undocumented.

00:03:14.131 --> 00:03:15.708
- It gave a lot of undocumented youth

00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:20.410
a sense of more freedom, and
it was hope for a lot of us.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.949
- This was the first time
when we suddenly felt

00:03:22.949 --> 00:03:25.612
a sense of belonging,
like all our hard work

00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:27.494
was finally about to pay off,

00:03:27.494 --> 00:03:31.317
and maybe lead to an opportunity
to access citizenship

00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:32.838
or a more long term solution.

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:35.724
- Not gonna happen because
of grass root community,

00:03:35.724 --> 00:03:38.656
it is undocumented folks
themselves who made DACA happen.

00:03:38.656 --> 00:03:40.284
There is hope, because a lot of people

00:03:40.284 --> 00:03:44.451
are just realizing, as we come
together, we'll find a way.

00:03:47.015 --> 00:03:48.350
- White House officials tell ABC News that

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.078
the president is seriously
considering ending a program

00:03:51.078 --> 00:03:55.065
that provides legal status
to hundreds of thousands

00:03:55.065 --> 00:03:58.330
of undocumented immigrants
who came to the United States

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.729
as children.

00:03:59.729 --> 00:04:01.604
- The move the president
is considering would put

00:04:01.604 --> 00:04:04.309
nearly 800,000 undocumented immigrants

00:04:04.309 --> 00:04:06.529
in danger of being deported.

00:04:06.529 --> 00:04:08.982
- In 2017, it's very hard to process

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.815
how you're able to live here.

00:04:11.815 --> 00:04:16.044
You grew up in this country
with friends, family,

00:04:16.044 --> 00:04:18.699
with this culture that you're used to,

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:22.430
and all of a sudden, the
country doesn't want you.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:26.592
- Knowing that DACA may
be repealed, has increased

00:04:26.592 --> 00:04:29.444
and heightened a lot of peoples' worries.

00:04:29.444 --> 00:04:31.644
- If DACA is removed, 800,000 people

00:04:31.644 --> 00:04:34.285
are going to go back to
a life of anxiety, fear,

00:04:34.285 --> 00:04:38.094
and uncertainty, because
they could lose their jobs,

00:04:38.094 --> 00:04:41.824
they might have to withdraw
from certain college programs.

00:04:41.824 --> 00:04:43.771
This could also mean that they are

00:04:43.771 --> 00:04:46.399
now that much more
vulnerable to deportation.

00:04:46.399 --> 00:04:48.427
- Immigration is a natural occurrence.

00:04:48.427 --> 00:04:50.374
It is going to happen,

00:04:50.374 --> 00:04:52.895
and we know that we have
to build up from it.

00:04:52.895 --> 00:04:54.530
We have seen progress in the past,

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.878
and just because there's
a little bit of reclining,

00:04:56.878 --> 00:04:59.152
it doesn't mean the
progress is gonna stop.

00:04:59.152 --> 00:05:02.102
- Our main goal is to
have what we deserve.

00:05:02.102 --> 00:05:04.291
We've been in this
country, we've worked hard,

00:05:04.291 --> 00:05:05.541
we belong here.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.999
- In the midst of all this,
I think that it's important

00:05:08.999 --> 00:05:11.853
to look around and realize that we have

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:14.844
such a big community
of advocates and allies

00:05:14.844 --> 00:05:16.818
that really want to see us succeed.

00:05:16.818 --> 00:05:19.104
Immigrants always find a way,

00:05:19.104 --> 00:05:21.565
and where there is no way, we create one.

00:05:21.565 --> 00:05:24.347
And I believe that that's
what's really made us so strong.

00:05:24.347 --> 00:05:26.343
We need to look to that same resilience

00:05:26.343 --> 00:05:28.433
to be able to get through what lies ahead

00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:30.303
by any means necessary.

00:05:30.303 --> 00:05:32.213
We're not gonna go anywhere,
and we just have to

00:05:32.213 --> 00:05:33.815
make sure that the rest of the country

00:05:33.815 --> 00:05:35.315
gets that message.

